---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReviewedByCard from "../../components/ReviewedByCard.astro";
import { TRUST_PROFILES } from "../../config/trust";

const title = "Mortgage Payoff Topic Guide (payment, amortization, extras)";
const description =
  "Mortgage payoff workflow: estimate the baseline payment, compare extra principal strategies, and choose the right decision or execution guide. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-04-06";
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/topics/mortgage-payoff"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  authorProfile={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
  reviewProfiles={[TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview, TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview]}
>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Topic</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/topics">Topics</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Mortgage payoff</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>Mortgage payment and payoff planning</h1>
    <p>
      Most mortgage payoff questions boil down to the same workflow: verify the baseline payment, compare extra-principal scenarios,
      and decide whether the better next step is a risk check, a payoff comparison, or an execution detail such as timing or posting.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/extra-payment-calculator">Extra payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/additional-principal-payment-calculator">Additional principal calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/amortization-schedule-calculator">Amortization schedule</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ReviewedByCard
    writtenBy={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
    reviewedBy={TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview}
    secondaryReview={TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview}
    reviewScope="Mortgage payoff topic routing, extra-payment decision-versus-execution guide structure, and calculator-to-guide workflow coverage."
    reviewedOn="2026-04-06"
  />

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Choose your mortgage payoff starting point</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Start with the <a href="/calculators/extra-payment-calculator">extra payment calculator</a> when you want to compare monthly extra, lump-sum, and target-payoff scenarios on the same loan baseline.</li>
      <li>Start with the <a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">mortgage payment calculator</a> or the <a href="/calculators/amortization-schedule-calculator">amortization schedule</a> if you still need to confirm the base payment and schedule first.</li>
      <li>Start with the decision or execution guides below if the real blocker is not the math itself, but whether extra payments are the right priority or whether they will be applied correctly.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Choose the extra-payment decision guide</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/extra-payment-liquidity-reserve">Liquidity reserve</a>: use this when cash reserves and emergency planning might matter more than a faster payoff.</li>
        <li><a href="/guides/extra-payment-priority-vs-other-debts">Priority vs other debts</a>: use this when credit cards or other higher-cost debt may deserve the extra cash first.</li>
        <li><a href="/guides/extra-payment-tax-deduction-impact">Tax deduction impact</a>: use this when after-tax assumptions are changing the payoff-versus-alternative comparison.</li>
        <li><a href="/guides/pay-off-mortgage-early-or-invest">Pay off early or invest?</a>: use this when the real decision is payoff certainty versus market-return uncertainty.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Choose the extra-payment execution guide</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/extra-payment-lump-sum-vs-monthly">Lump sum vs monthly</a>: use this when timing is the reason two equal-dollar plans may not save the same amount.</li>
        <li><a href="/guides/extra-payment-target-payoff-date">Target payoff date</a>: use this when you have a mortgage-free deadline and need to reverse-engineer a realistic monthly extra.</li>
        <li><a href="/guides/extra-payment-servicer-posting-rules">Servicer posting rules</a>: use this when statement behavior or paid-ahead treatment makes the savings hard to trust.</li>
        <li><a href="/guides/principal-only-extra-payments">Principal-only extra payments</a> and <a href="/guides/one-extra-mortgage-payment-per-year">one extra payment per year</a>: use these when the plan is chosen and the remaining question is how to execute it correctly.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Core payoff workflow</h2>
    <ol class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Confirm your current balance, note rate, remaining term, and whether your statement reflects principal-only extra payments correctly.</li>
      <li>Model the baseline first so every extra-payment scenario uses the same starting assumptions.</li>
      <li>Run the decision layer if reserves, higher-cost debt, taxes, or investing alternatives could change the answer.</li>
      <li>Run the execution layer after the decision is made so timing, target dates, and servicer behavior do not distort the result.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Core calculators</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/amortization-schedule-calculator">Amortization schedule</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/extra-payment-calculator">Extra payment calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/additional-principal-payment-calculator">Additional principal calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related payoff comparisons</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/biweekly-vs-extra-principal">Biweekly vs extra principal</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/mortgage-recast-vs-extra-payments">Recast vs extra payments</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/pmi-removal-vs-extra-principal">PMI removal vs extra principal</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/extra-mortgage-payments">Extra mortgage payments</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mortgage-payoff mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Comparing extra-payment scenarios without first locking the same baseline balance, rate, and remaining term.</li>
      <li>Ignoring liquidity, competing debt, or tax treatment and assuming mortgage payoff is always the best extra use of cash.</li>
      <li>Trusting a calculator result without confirming the servicer posts the extra payment to principal the way the model assumes.</li>
      <li>Using long-term savings headlines when the real time horizon is short because a refinance or move is likely.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">References</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/consumer-tools/mortgages/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Mortgage resources
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/ask-cfpb/how-do-i-manage-my-monthly-mortgage-payment-en-1825/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          How do I manage my monthly mortgage payment?
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/ask-cfpb/what-is-a-prepayment-penalty-en-1957/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          What is a prepayment penalty?
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/extra-payment-calculator">Start the payoff model</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/extra-payment-liquidity-reserve">Check decision risks</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/extra-payment-servicer-posting-rules">Check execution risks</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-04-06</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
